# Load balancers

## Certificates

`nemau_load_balancer_certificate` sends `private_key` once. The API never
returns it, so Terraform keeps the configured value in state and the resource
cannot be imported. Keep the state encrypted.

Every attribute forces a replacement, and names are unique within a project.
Set `name_prefix` instead of `name` (a unique name is generated at each
replacement, as with `aws_acm_certificate`) together with
`create_before_destroy`. A renewal then imports the new certificate, moves the
listener's `tls_certificate_ref` to it in place, and deletes the old one.

```terraform
resource "nemau_load_balancer_certificate" "www" {
  name_prefix = "www-"
  certificate = file("${path.module}/fullchain.pem")
  private_key = file("${path.module}/privkey.pem")

  lifecycle {
    create_before_destroy = true
  }
}

resource "nemau_listener" "https" {
  load_balancer_id    = nemau_load_balancer.edge.id
  name                = "https"
  protocol            = "TERMINATED_HTTPS"
  protocol_port       = 443
  default_pool_id     = nemau_pool.web.id
  tls_certificate_ref = nemau_load_balancer_certificate.www.id
}
```

To renew, replace the two files and apply.

The [HTTPS load balancer example](https://github.com/nemau-cloud/terraform-provider-nemau/tree/main/examples/https-load-balancer)
terminates HTTPS on a load balancer and forwards plain HTTP to a pool.

## Engine

The engine cannot be chosen. Every new `nemau_load_balancer` runs in automatic
mode and accepts `HTTP`, `HTTPS`, `TCP` and `UDP` listeners side by side. The
read-only `provider_engine` attribute reports the engine (`provider` is a
reserved name in Terraform). It reads `auto` on every load balancer this
provider creates; an older load balancer that was imported may report `haproxy`
(no `UDP` listeners) or `nginx` (`UDP` listeners only).

## High-availability tiers

On `lb-ha`, `lb-medium` and `lb-large`, health checks and proxied connections
leave from each appliance's own address rather than from the VIP.
`appliance_addresses` lists those addresses (on `lb-small` it holds the VIP
alone). Allow them in the members' security groups.

The tier is chosen at creation. Changing `flavor` replaces the load balancer
and allocates a new VIP.
